# Production build-time env. Vite loads this automatically for
# `vite build` (production mode) and it overrides .env. These values are
# inlined into the PUBLIC client bundle at build time — they are not
# secret (the browser sees them), so this file is committed.
#
# Why it must live here and not in the Pages dashboard: `npm run deploy`
# runs `vite build` on your machine, so the bundle is baked locally.
# Cloudflare Pages dashboard env vars only apply when CF builds from git;
# a local build never sees them. The API is a different origin from this
# frontend (see docs/DEPLOY.md) — point at the Worker's custom domain.
# One origin drives fetch, Replicache, and the websocket; https here means
# the ws endpoint becomes wss:// (src/lib/config.js).
VITE_DJIBB_ORIGIN=https://api.djibb.com
